  "description": "THE ACCOUNT-BREAK ORDER, made visible. 1050-UPDATE-ACCOUNT is four statements at :352-356 and all four are asserted here: ADD WS-TOTAL-INT TO ACCT-CURR-BAL, MOVE 0 TO ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT, MOVE 0 TO ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT, then REWRITE. The seeded account 1 carries NON-ZERO cycle amounts - 123.45 credit and 678.90 debit, replacing the fixture's zeros - which is the only way the two MOVEs are observable at all: against the fixture's own 00000000000{ spans, zeroing them is a no-op and the assertion cannot fail. The rewritten image therefore shows 206.50 in ACCT-CURR-BAL and 00000000000{ in both cycle spans, and every other byte of the 300 - the misspelled ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE at offset 59, ACCT-ADDR-ZIP's A000000000 at 103, the trailing FILLER X(178) - is carried through verbatim. Order matters and is pinned by the value: the interest is added to the BALANCE and not to a cycle amount, and the cycle amounts are cleared rather than accumulated into.",
